Virtual functions and a virtual destructor across a virtual base shared by
two bases: dispatch through V*, B1* and B2& reaches the most derived
overrider (thunks adjust `this' by the virtual base's offset in the
complete object), a virtual-base member is read through the vtable's
virtual-base offset (Itanium C++ ABI 2.5.2), V is constructed and
destroyed exactly once per complete object (N5008 [class.base.init]/13,
[class.dtor]/14: by the most derived class, via the hidden `@most_derived'
constructor/destructor parameter), and both bases' constructors update the
single V.
